{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788129975,"nonce":"wdX1BwsG/9exxJiiQS6EqqzuV/s=","message":"UNDECLARED ADDITION, declared — four fixture steps on `journal-selftest`.\n\nSame precedent, same shape and the same disclosure duty as 2.1's `stockpile`\nstep: they live inside `journal-selftest`, keep the `Prefs.DevMode` gate, journal\none `dev` event per step for provenance, and 3.1's dev layer supersedes them.\nThree of this spec's acceptance lines need game state no shipped verb can create\nand 3.1 does not exist yet.\n\n`alerts` / `alerts-clear` — args `alert_count` (default 15),\n`alert_critical_last` (default true).\nInjects Alert instances straight into `AlertsReadout.activeAlerts`: the same\nlist the game draws from and the same list `AlertScanner.Snapshot` reads, so the\ndigest's new sort runs against real readout state and not a stub. Safe by\nconstruction rather than by hope — the fixture types subclass `Alert_Custom` /\n`Alert_CustomCritical`, and AlertsReadout's constructor EXCLUDES both from\n`allAlertTypesCached` (decompiled AlertsReadout.cs:64), so the game never\ninstantiates them, never polls them, and its round-robin\n`CheckAddOrRemoveAlert` never removes ours either. They cost nothing when the\nfixture is not running. The critical subclass overrides `DoMessage =\u003e false`,\nbecause `Alert_Critical.AlertActiveUpdate` fires a ThreatBig message every other\nframe and a fixture proving a SORT must not flood the journal to do it.\n`alerts-clear` removes them again.\n\n`colonists` — arg `colonist_target` (default 20).\n`PawnGenerator.GeneratePawn(PawnKindDefOf.Colonist, Faction.OfPlayer)` +\n`GenSpawn.Spawn` at `CellFinder.RandomClosewalkCellNear`, up to the target\nheadcount. Returns before/spawned/now.\n\n`power` — args `power_lamps` (default 1), `power_fuel` (75), `power_stored`\n(300), `power_generator` (true).\nBuilds one real grid: a conduit run with a wood-fired generator\n(basePowerConsumption -1000, i.e. 1000 W produced), a battery (600 Wd cap) and N\nstanding lamps at 30 W each, all cardinally adjacent to the conduits so they\nform one net. Buildings get `SetFactionDirect(Faction.OfPlayer)` before spawn,\nthe game's own dev-spawn route, so power nets and `DeconstructibleBy` both see\nthe player's faction. It returns `expect_gen_w` / `expect_draw_w` derived from\nthe DEF XML — an independent hand-computation for the digest's live\n`PowerNet.powerComps` walk to agree with, the same two-readers-one-truth\ndiscipline 2.1's `stockpile` step used.\n\nTwo of its knobs exist to reach cases that are otherwise unreachable:\n`power_fuel:0` gives the deficit case (`CompPowerPlant.UpdateDesiredPowerOutput`\nzeroes PowerOutput with no fuel), which is the only state where `battery_days`\nmeans anything; `power_generator:false` gives the battery-only grid that exposes\nthe `nets` rider.\n\nOne helper came with them, `FindClearRect` — first unfogged, standable,\nedifice-free, heavy-affordance w x h footprint outward from the anchor. It fails\nloudly rather than falling back to a cell that will not hold a grid.","files":null}]}